1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,400
In this video you will start a game from the list, move it between console memory

2
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:10,600
and the microSD card, dump it as NSP files, delete it, and create a save slot.

3
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:12,600
Open Tools, Game Tools, Games.

4
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:14,600
Each game has small tags.

5
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:19,533
SD or NAND shows where it is stored, and Base, Update and DLC show what is

6
00:00:19,533 --> 00:00:21,533
installed.

7
00:00:21,533 --> 00:00:26,467
To start a game, highlight it and press L3, that is, click the left stick.

8
00:00:26,467 --> 00:00:28,467
Not sure what to play?

9
00:00:28,467 --> 00:00:32,933
Press plus, choose "Launch random game", then Launch in the window.

10
00:00:32,933 --> 00:00:34,933
A opens Game Details.

11
00:00:34,933 --> 00:00:39,600
At the top: the Title ID, version, play time and when you last played.

12
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:43,400
At the bottom are three tabs: Content, Tickets and Saves.

13
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:45,600
Switch between them with L and R.

14
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:48,400
ZL and ZR go to the previous or next game.

15
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:53,467
On the Content tab, the base game, the update and the DLC are separate rows.

16
00:00:53,467 --> 00:00:57,067
Now let's move a game from console memory to the card.

17
00:00:57,067 --> 00:01:02,600
Kefir Hub first copies the game, switches it to the new copy, and only then deletes

18
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:04,600
the old one.

19
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:09,733
On the details screen press plus, and under Game Actions choose "Move to SD".

20
00:01:09,733 --> 00:01:13,533
Only the direction that has something to move is offered.

21
00:01:13,533 --> 00:01:19,067
The summary shows what will move, what stays, the total size, and the free space on

22
00:01:19,067 --> 00:01:21,133
both storages before and after.

23
00:01:21,133 --> 00:01:23,133
Choose Move.

24
00:01:23,133 --> 00:01:26,733
If there is not enough space, the move does not start.

25
00:01:26,733 --> 00:01:29,733
While data is being copied you can cancel it.

26
00:01:29,733 --> 00:01:35,267
At the last step, when the game switches to the new copy, you can no longer cancel.

27
00:01:35,267 --> 00:01:38,067
Do not turn the console off during a move.

28
00:01:38,067 --> 00:01:43,533
To move several games, use the list: select them with X, press plus and choose the

29
00:01:43,533 --> 00:01:45,533
direction.

30
00:01:45,533 --> 00:01:48,933
The move then starts right away, without a summary.

31
00:01:48,933 --> 00:01:52,800
You can also move just one part, for example only the DLC.

32
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:58,267
On the Content tab press A on its row and choose "Move component to NAND" or "Move

33
00:01:58,267 --> 00:02:00,267
component to SD".

34
00:02:00,267 --> 00:02:03,000
Next, a dump: saving a game as NSP files.

35
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:07,200
Highlight a game or select several, press plus and choose Dump.

36
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:12,733
Choose what to dump: "Dump All", "Dump Application" for the base game, "Dump Patch"

37
00:02:12,733 --> 00:02:15,867
for the update, or "Dump AddOnContent" for DLC.

38
00:02:15,867 --> 00:02:19,800
In "Select dump location", choose "microSD card (/dumps/)".

39
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:23,333
The files appear in the dumps/NSP folder on the card.

40
00:02:23,333 --> 00:02:28,000
You can install these files again later, as shown in the second video.

41
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:33,200
The same list also offers a USB transfer to another console, plus your network

42
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:35,200
locations and USB drives.

43
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:37,400
You can also build a single file.

44
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:41,400
On the details screen press plus and choose "Create repack".

45
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:46,933
Tick "Application/BASE", "Patch/Update" and "AddOnContent/DLC", then choose "Create

46
00:02:46,933 --> 00:02:48,933
repack" at the bottom.

47
00:02:48,933 --> 00:02:52,200
The file appears in the games folder on the card.

48
00:02:52,200 --> 00:02:57,467
To delete a game, highlight it or select several, press plus, choose Delete and

49
00:02:57,467 --> 00:02:59,467
confirm with Delete.

50
00:02:59,467 --> 00:03:02,333
The base game, updates and DLC are deleted.

51
00:03:02,333 --> 00:03:06,667
The saves stay: you find them in Saves, on the Deleted Games tab.

52
00:03:06,667 --> 00:03:09,933
To remove them too, delete them there separately.

53
00:03:09,933 --> 00:03:14,600
The Saves tab in Game Details manages the saves on the console itself.

54
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:18,667
X creates an empty save for a user who does not have one yet.

55
00:03:18,667 --> 00:03:22,867
Pick the user, then the size: standard, plus 16 or plus 64 MiB.

56
00:03:22,867 --> 00:03:25,267
Check the summary and choose Create.

57
00:03:25,267 --> 00:03:30,667
For several games at once: select them in the list, press plus and choose "Create

58
00:03:30,667 --> 00:03:32,667
save".

59
00:03:32,667 --> 00:03:38,133
Kefir Hub creates a standard save for the chosen user and skips games that already

60
00:03:38,133 --> 00:03:40,133
have one.

61
00:03:40,133 --> 00:03:42,733
"Increase save size" adds 16 or 64 MiB.

62
00:03:42,733 --> 00:03:45,533
You cannot make a save smaller afterwards.

63
00:03:45,533 --> 00:03:49,067
"Backup and restore" opens Saves with only this game.

64
00:03:49,067 --> 00:03:52,067
The previous video shows how to make backups.

65
00:03:52,067 --> 00:03:55,600
The Mods folder line shows whether the game has mods.

66
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:59,267
Plus, "Open mods folder", opens it in the File Browser.

67
00:03:59,267 --> 00:04:03,067
An empty folder does nothing; copy the mod files into it.

68
00:04:03,067 --> 00:04:07,200
The plus menu on the list also has Layout, Sort By and Search.

69
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:11,067
Type part of a name to find a game quickly in a long list.

70
00:04:11,067 --> 00:04:15,267
To sort by play time, first choose Sort By, "Update play time".

71
00:04:15,267 --> 00:04:18,800
Kefir Hub reads the play time from the console's log.

72
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:22,200
For more, read the Games page in the documentation.
